1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:06,423
You cheating bastard!

2
00:00:06,506 --> 00:00:07,340
What?

3
00:00:07,424 --> 00:00:10,593
You're the worst! Apologize to your wife!

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,011
I didn't do it.

5
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:13,263
<i>I did not have an affair.</i>

6
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:15,724
<i>That article is a complete lie.</i>

7
00:00:17,892 --> 00:00:19,144
Jin Ichijo.

8
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:21,438
Surrounded by young girls
on a harem vacation

9
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:23,231
in the middle of a major scandal…

10
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:27,652
Are you leaving already?

11
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:30,530
<i>Something has been bothering me.</i>

12
00:00:30,613 --> 00:00:31,656
Enough!

13
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,908
Stop looking at the Internet.

14
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:35,952
It's so delicious.

15
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:37,120
Shall we drink?

16
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:40,498
Vacation is the best!

17
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:42,792
Just how angry is your wife?

18
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:45,754
A scorned woman's revenge is terrifying.

19
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:47,464
What? Who is it?

20
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:49,841
Who is it?!

21
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:52,761
Who might you be?

22
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:54,429
I am…

23
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:56,806
Jin Ichijo's wife.

24
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:00,185
Is…

25
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:02,437
my husband here?

26
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:08,485
All set.

27
00:01:13,823 --> 00:01:15,617
Here you go.

28
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:25,752
To think his wife would come here…

29
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:27,378
How did she even find this place?

30
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:29,130
Maybe she put a GPS tracker on him?

31
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:32,759
What? You mean he was cheating
all over with a GPS attached to him?

32
00:01:32,842 --> 00:01:35,011
Old-school actors are like that,
didn't you know?

33
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:36,513
What are we going to do?

34
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:38,723
This will be a bloodbath.

35
00:01:47,649 --> 00:01:51,277
This is a compote made from
the summer oranges in our garden.

36
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:53,822
Please try it.

37
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:58,827
Midori, when did you make this?

38
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:01,037
I think I made it yesterday while drunk.

39
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,247
I don't really remember.

40
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:24,060
It's good.

41
00:02:27,772 --> 00:02:30,400
So you can pick summer oranges
in the garden…

42
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:33,778
What a wonderful villa.

43
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:36,030
Thank you.

44
00:02:36,114 --> 00:02:39,075
This villa was left behind
by my grandmother.

45
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:42,662
We thought we could spend the summer here.

46
00:02:42,745 --> 00:02:45,707
That's right. We all happen to be
unemployed right now.

47
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:48,710
It's what you would call
a vacation from life!

48
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:51,921
Vacation…

49
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:57,135
You too. You came here…

50
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:02,015
to take a vacation, didn't you?

51
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:06,811
No, it's not like that.

52
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:11,024
I just wanted to escape from the media.

53
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:35,715
What are you trying to do?

54
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:43,139
Human issues have nothing
to do with us, right?

55
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:45,433
Sea God.

56
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:49,812
SEA GOD

57
00:03:49,896 --> 00:03:53,358
It's best not to stick your nose
into human affairs.

58
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:55,109
You…

59
00:03:55,902 --> 00:04:00,073
do you know who that man really is?

60
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:04,744
Weekly Shuubun<i>.</i>

61
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:09,624
A magazine that makes money
week after week off celebrity scandals.

62
00:04:11,209 --> 00:04:14,587
Humans all have secrets, after all.

63
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:17,715
They expose those secrets
to make a profit.

64
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:21,886
Sometimes, they even end up
taking people's lives.

65
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,681
They're basically like demons.

66
00:04:25,556 --> 00:04:28,893
Though, saying that
to a Grim Reaper is a bit strange.

67
00:04:32,689 --> 00:04:33,690
Yes.

68
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:11,728
Ryoko.

69
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:16,190
I have truly caused you so much trouble.

70
00:05:16,274 --> 00:05:17,650
I'm at your mercy!

71
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,193
I am so sorry!

72
00:05:19,277 --> 00:05:20,153
He's groveling!

73
00:05:20,236 --> 00:05:23,156
The poor wife! This is just too painful.

74
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:25,950
If it's come to this, she should just get
a big payout and divorce him.

75
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:27,243
The wife is crying.

76
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,078
This situation is terrible.

77
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:30,079
Konta.

78
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:32,248
-What?
-Are we doing a barbecue tonight?

79
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:34,292
-Will his wife want some?
-Are you stupid?

80
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:38,046
This is no time for that! As Rinrin said,
a scorned woman's revenge is terrifying!

81
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:40,173
Mr. Jin may just get stabbed!

82
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:43,009
-Maybe we should hide the kitchen knives.
-Maybe.

83
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,303
I…

84
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:47,430
I'm so ashamed.

85
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:51,225
At this age, to be humiliated like this…

86
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:54,520
This is hell.

87
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:57,607
A living hell!

88
00:05:58,107 --> 00:05:59,275
I'm at fault.

89
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:01,527
I am at your mercy!

90
00:06:02,195 --> 00:06:07,366
I didn't think I would be caught
by <i>Shuubun</i>, hugging on the street.

91
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:10,912
And it wasn't…

92
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:14,332
just once, you know!

93
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:17,502
It was three times!

94
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:18,503
That hurts.

95
00:06:19,295 --> 00:06:20,421
Three times!

96
00:06:20,505 --> 00:06:22,131
Why didn't you notice?

97
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:24,884
Your guard was way too low! Idiot!

98
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:27,845
Ryoko, I am at your mercy!

99
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,222
I am so sorry!

100
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:31,849
Idiot.

101
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:33,810
Idiot!

102
00:06:36,896 --> 00:06:38,106
-Idiot!
-I'm sorry!

103
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:41,567
-Idiot! Don't run!
-I'm sorry!

104
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:42,985
What should we do?

105
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:44,487
Let's hide the knives!

106
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:46,823
Let's hide everything
that could be used as a weapon.

107
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:48,157
Hide them! What is there?

108
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:50,409
Should we hide this too?

109
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:54,664
Hey! You look like a serial killer!

110
00:06:54,747 --> 00:06:57,041
The wife might have brought
a weapon with her.

111
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:59,836
-Let's take away her bag!
-The bag!

112
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:01,420
You absolute fool!

113
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:03,631
Idiot!

114
00:07:03,714 --> 00:07:06,175
You! You absolute idiot!

115
00:07:06,259 --> 00:07:07,927
Okay!

116
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:09,846
Idiot!

117
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:15,184
-Check if there's a weapon inside!
-Yes!

118
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:17,520
Okay!

119
00:07:21,482 --> 00:07:22,483
What is this?

120
00:07:24,235 --> 00:07:25,486
Yes.

121
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:28,656
The second article
will be a hit with this, Chief Editor.

122
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:31,784
The cheating piece of trash
Jin Ichijo shows no remorse!

123
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:34,996
Gathering <i>gyaru </i>at a Tatsumi Town villa
for a harem drinking party!

124
00:07:35,997 --> 00:07:38,916
Let's hit him hard this week too!

125
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,210
Let's keep the fire going!

126
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:46,007
-Do you enjoy lighting fires?
-Whoa!

127
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:47,425
What the hell?

128
00:07:48,509 --> 00:07:50,595
Oh, you're the guy from before…

129
00:07:51,512 --> 00:07:52,555
What?

130
00:07:53,264 --> 00:07:55,933
Are you one of Jin Ichijo's
actor buddies or something?

131
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:57,310
Huh?

132
00:07:57,393 --> 00:08:01,898
I, too, like to set things on fire.

133
00:08:02,648 --> 00:08:03,858
What?

134
00:08:07,069 --> 00:08:08,571
Hot, that's hot!

135
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:10,323
So hot! It's burning!

136
00:08:10,406 --> 00:08:12,200
Why? So hot!

137
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:13,451
Why?

138
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:14,368
So hot!

139
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:16,120
-Is it on fire?
-So hot!

140
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:18,289
-So hot!
-Well then, let's put it out.

141
00:08:22,793 --> 00:08:24,420
Nice underhand throw!

142
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:26,547
Wait, no. Bad, that's bad.

143
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:30,426
What did you do?

144
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:31,761
Why did you throw it?

145
00:08:31,844 --> 00:08:33,304
Why did you throw my camera?

146
00:08:33,387 --> 00:08:36,140
Who the hell are you working for?

147
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:37,600
Just what are you?

148
00:08:38,309 --> 00:08:41,562
I'm the same breed as you guys.

149
00:08:48,277 --> 00:08:49,445
Oh, it's so cute!

150
00:08:49,529 --> 00:08:50,988
You're like an idol.

151
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:53,574
Where did you buy this, ma'am?

152
00:08:53,658 --> 00:08:55,576
-I want one too.
-Go on!

153
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:57,787
Did you rummage through my bag?

154
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:00,206
This is yours, isn't it, ma'am?

155
00:09:01,457 --> 00:09:03,459
No! Um…

156
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:04,544
Was it in there?

157
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:07,880
No, I have no intention of using it.

158
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:09,882
It's just, you know, just in case…

159
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:15,096
You never know what might happen, right?

160
00:09:15,179 --> 00:09:17,598
What do you mean "just in case"?
What case?

161
00:09:17,682 --> 00:09:20,309
-By just in case, I mean…
-There's other stuff too!

162
00:09:20,393 --> 00:09:23,396
-Stop it!
-Stop it! Don't look!

163
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:25,481
This…

164
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:28,150
Wait, so those photos…

165
00:09:28,734 --> 00:09:30,945
<i>They were all you, ma'am?</i>

166
00:09:31,529 --> 00:09:33,739
Seriously?

167
00:09:34,323 --> 00:09:36,492
No! Stop it!

168
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:38,536
We're busted!

169
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:40,037
Stop it!

170
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:44,709
-Ryoko!
-Darling!

171
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:48,254
<i>Ryoko!</i>

172
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:50,047
<i>Yes!</i>

173
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:52,091
<i>What do you like?</i>

174
00:09:52,174 --> 00:09:54,135
<i>Chocolate mint, but more than that…</i>

175
00:09:54,218 --> 00:09:55,678
<i>I like you!</i>

176
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:04,312
T-This means…

177
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:05,896
To spice up their marriage,

178
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:10,026
the wife dressed up and role-played
as different types of women.

179
00:10:10,109 --> 00:10:12,903
And they were
going on dates out in the city?

180
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:14,572
Then they got photographed?

181
00:10:14,655 --> 00:10:16,866
Then you should just tell everyone that!

182
00:10:16,949 --> 00:10:19,910
You weren't cheating with several women,
it was all your wife!

183
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:22,163
How could I possibly say that?

184
00:10:22,747 --> 00:10:24,373
Making my wife, at this age,

185
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:28,002
do all kinds of cosplay
and wander around the city…

186
00:10:28,085 --> 00:10:32,632
If her parents or our relatives
found out about that, we…

187
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:35,926
we would both die of embarrassment!

188
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:38,471
That's one "we" too many, darling.

189
00:10:38,554 --> 00:10:39,972
That's not true at all!

190
00:10:40,806 --> 00:10:42,433
It's a wonderful thing!

191
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:43,976
You two want to date

192
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:46,854
while keeping things fresh,
just like when you were young.

193
00:10:46,937 --> 00:10:49,440
That means you're putting effort
into your marriage!

194
00:10:49,523 --> 00:10:51,609
That's right, it's lovely!

195
00:10:51,692 --> 00:10:54,779
That is what true love is.
You're the ideal couple!

196
00:10:54,862 --> 00:10:57,031
If you can liven things up
with idol cosplay,

197
00:10:57,114 --> 00:10:58,407
do it as much as you want!

198
00:10:58,491 --> 00:11:01,327
Jin, let's announce this to the world.

199
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:04,080
Prove to your sponsors
and the film industry

200
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:06,248
that you weren't four-timing anyone!

201
00:11:06,832 --> 00:11:07,667
Okay.

202
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,418
What a great couple!

203
00:11:09,502 --> 00:11:11,504
-What are you doing?
-You look great together.

204
00:11:11,587 --> 00:11:15,966
Mr. Jin, ma'am,
let's tell everyone the truth.

205
00:11:17,343 --> 00:11:18,677
Everyone?

206
00:11:30,898 --> 00:11:32,149
What is it?

207
00:11:32,858 --> 00:11:36,153
What the hell do you want?

208
00:11:36,237 --> 00:11:38,322
No!

209
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:42,535
Hold on!

210
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:50,751
Hey! Hold on! Help me!

211
00:11:50,835 --> 00:11:53,337
It's better than going to hell, right?

212
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:55,089
Come on!

213
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:58,008
Help me! Wait!

214
00:11:58,092 --> 00:11:59,593
Help!

215
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:01,137
No!

216
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:04,932
Help me! Hey! Wait!

217
00:12:05,015 --> 00:12:07,726
Hey! Come back!

218
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:18,237
I guess I should report this
to the higher-ups.

219
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:27,329
I've got this, calm down.

220
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:28,956
<i>Like this?</i>

221
00:12:29,039 --> 00:12:30,332
<i>Is it rolling already?</i>

222
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:32,042
<i>It has started.</i>

223
00:12:32,126 --> 00:12:33,919
<i>Well, um…</i>

224
00:12:34,587 --> 00:12:39,133
<i>regarding the recent incident</i>
<i>that's causing a stir,</i>

225
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:42,720
<i>I, Jin Ichijo, and my wife,</i>
<i>would like to talk about it.</i>

226
00:12:44,722 --> 00:12:47,141
<i>I am so sorry that my husband</i>

227
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:53,772
<i>was suspected of cheating,</i>
<i>and it caused quite a ruckus.</i>

228
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:58,068
<i>You see, the truth is,</i>

229
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:02,573
<i>all of those women were me.</i>

230
00:13:03,407 --> 00:13:08,621
I asked my wife to do cosplay,

231
00:13:08,704 --> 00:13:13,709
and we went out on dates together.

232
00:13:13,792 --> 00:13:17,129
So, this wasn't an affair.

233
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:19,089
<i>We are husband and wife.</i>

234
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:21,842
<i>-Yes. We're very sorry.</i>
<i>-We're very sorry.</i>

235
00:13:21,926 --> 00:13:24,053
<i>We apologize for the commotion.</i>

236
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:27,473
Now, this is the correct way
to use the Internet!

237
00:13:27,556 --> 00:13:29,517
Everyone is being so supportive!

238
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:31,852
Oh, we just got a Super Chat.

239
00:13:32,561 --> 00:13:33,646
Look.

240
00:13:33,729 --> 00:13:36,106
They're saying,
"You're a wonderful couple."

241
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:37,775
"Sorry for the misunderstanding."

242
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:39,568
Wow, goodness…

243
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:41,070
I'm so happy.

244
00:13:41,153 --> 00:13:43,531
-How kind. Thank you so much.
-Thank you.

245
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:48,786
<i>And, this broadcast was brought to you</i>
<i>by the next big thing, Konta Hoshino!</i>

246
00:13:48,869 --> 00:13:50,204
<i>The light is too close!</i>

247
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:52,581
<i>Brought to you by…</i>

248
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,208
<i>-Hey now!</i>
<i>-I'm sorry!</i>

249
00:13:55,709 --> 00:13:56,919
<i>Too close!</i>

250
00:13:58,462 --> 00:14:00,339
<i>You're in the shot.</i>

251
00:14:01,465 --> 00:14:02,841
<i>How lovely.</i>

252
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:05,469
They're a great couple, aren't they?

253
00:14:05,553 --> 00:14:07,721
Even if they go a bit overboard.

254
00:14:07,805 --> 00:14:09,223
Going overboard is fine.

255
00:14:09,306 --> 00:14:10,933
I want to get married too.

256
00:14:11,016 --> 00:14:16,855
Get married and be a lovey-dovey
couple forever, just like them!

257
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:17,940
Exactly.

258
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:22,027
We're on a hard-earned vacation,
so we've got to find some romance.

259
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:28,701
We can't just be drinking stupid booze
and getting wasted every time.

260
00:14:28,784 --> 00:14:30,411
Romance, huh.

261
00:14:30,494 --> 00:14:32,997
Midori, you seriously
need to get a boyfriend soon!

262
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:36,208
Not having dated a guy at your age
is honestly a red flag!

263
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:39,628
Let's invite some guys over
and have a mixer at this villa!

264
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:40,546
What?

265
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:42,673
A mixer at the villa…

266
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:44,425
That sounds just like
a reality show. I love it.

267
00:14:44,508 --> 00:14:45,509
A reality show?

268
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:46,969
Like a dating show?

269
00:14:47,052 --> 00:14:48,762
I hate that, no way!

270
00:14:48,846 --> 00:14:50,431
-No.
-But, wait…

271
00:14:53,809 --> 00:14:56,478
<i>Mr. Nishigami. I wonder where he went.</i>

272
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:24,548
<i>I wonder if I'm even capable</i>
<i>of falling in love.</i>

273
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:52,326
So today is…

274
00:15:53,452 --> 00:15:55,329
Yes! It’s a girls' day.

275
00:15:55,412 --> 00:15:58,207
-Well then…
-Oh, wait…

276
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:01,877
I wonder where everyone meets
their soulmates.

277
00:16:01,961 --> 00:16:04,338
The new season of <i>Last Princess</i>
is streaming!

278
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:06,006
All right, let’s watch it! Right now!

279
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:08,801
I'm in the mood for romance,
so we are watching this now!

280
00:16:09,385 --> 00:16:10,761
I'm Kotaro Komiyama.

281
00:16:10,844 --> 00:16:12,596
This guy seems super shady.

282
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,306
I'm 27 years old.

283
00:16:14,390 --> 00:16:15,641
I'm a cheerleader.

284
00:16:15,724 --> 00:16:17,142
I'm attending a training school.

285
00:16:17,226 --> 00:16:18,435
It’s clout chasing.

286
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:20,062
I bet it's scripted.

287
00:16:20,145 --> 00:16:22,940
Midori! If you talk like that,
you can't enjoy dating shows!

288
00:16:23,023 --> 00:16:24,191
Excuse me.

289
00:16:24,274 --> 00:16:25,901
Who are you?

290
00:16:26,485 --> 00:16:27,444
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
